  "title": "Measurement of Peak XV",
  "summary": "After about four years of checking, Andrew Waugh of the Survey of India announced in March 1856 that Peak XV stood 29,002 feet high. The figure came from the mean of six calculated altitudes, worked out by chief computer Radhanath Sikdar's team. Peak XV was later known as Everest.",
